&lt;div class="content-intro"&gt;&lt;p&gt;Acme Robotics builds autonomy software for warehouse fleets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;script&gt;window.__gh = 1;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work on the fleet scheduling service, written in &lt;strong&gt;Go&lt;/strong&gt; and backed by &lt;strong&gt;PostgreSQL&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Redis&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS or MS in Computer Science, graduating between December 2026 and June 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a statically typed language such as Go, Java, or C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with relational databases and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Docker &amp;amp; Kubernetes is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Distributed systems coursework&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Open source contributions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We sponsor H-1B and TN visas for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
